  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "NNN line segments (numbered 111 through NNN) are placed on the 2D2D2D-plane. For each valid iii, the iii-th segment starts at Ai⃗=(xi,yi)\\vec{A_i} = (x_i, y_i)Ai​​=(xi​,yi​) and ends at Bi⃗=(Xi,Yi)\\vec{B_i} = (X_i, Y_i)Bi​​=(Xi​,Yi​). Line segments can move with a velocity of  magnitude 1 unit/sec along the direction of vector (Ai⃗−Bi⃗)(\\vec{A_i} - \\vec{B_i})(Ai​​−Bi​​) or  (Bi⃗−Ai⃗)(\\vec{B_i} - \\vec{A_i})(Bi​​−Ai​​).\n\nAt the time t=0t = 0t=0, all segments start moving for each valid iii. You need to assign a direction to the movement of each segment (not necessarily the same for all segments), such that there is no time from t=0t = 0t=0 to t=1010000t = 10^{10000}t=1010000 (both inclusive) when any two segments touch or intersect each other.\n\nDecide if it is possible to assign directions to the segments in such a way that the above condition is satisfied.\n\n###Input:\n\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT, the number of testcases.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nNNN lines follow,. For each iii (1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N), the iii-th of these lines contains four space-separated integers xix_ixi​, yiy_iyi​, XiX_iXi​, YiY_iYi​.\n###Output:\nFor each test case, print a single line containing the string `\"YES\"` if it is possible to assign the directions in a valid way or `\"NO\"` if it is impossible.\n\n###Constraints\n\n\n1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000\n1≤N≤20001 \\leq N \\leq 20001≤N≤2000\nSum of NNN over all testcases ≤2000\\leq 2000≤2000\nAbsolute value of coordinates of all points ≤106\\leq 10^6≤106\nAll input points in a single testcase are distinct",
    "constraints": [],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
